\section{The identity}

The default User-Agent names the tool, its version and where to read
about it.
It deliberately carries no contact address, although the polite-pool
convention suggests one.
The User-Agent goes with \emph{every} request, so an address in it
would reach every host scholar contacts, a publisher's server during a
PDF download included, and the services that want an address already
get [[SCHOLAR_EMAIL]] through their own channel: OpenAlex and Crossref
as the [[mailto]] parameter of their polite pools, Unpaywall as its
mandatory [[email]] parameter (\cref{sec:contact-email}).
Keeping the address out of the User-Agent therefore costs those
services nothing and tells everyone else nothing.
A user who does want it everywhere can set [[SCHOLAR_USER_AGENT]].

The version comes from the installed distribution's metadata (the
package is published as [[scholarcli]]); a source tree that was never
installed reports [[unknown]] rather than failing.

<<user agent>>=
def scholar_version() -> str:
    """Return the installed scholar version, or `"unknown"`."""
    try:
        return importlib.metadata.version(DISTRIBUTION_NAME)
    except importlib.metadata.PackageNotFoundError:
        return "unknown"


def default_user_agent() -> str:
    """Return scholar's own User-Agent: name, version and home page."""
    return f"scholar/{scholar_version()} (+{PROJECT_URL})"


def user_agent() -> str:
    """Return the User-Agent for scholar's requests.

    `SCHOLAR_USER_AGENT` overrides the default.
    """
    return os.environ.get(USER_AGENT_VAR, "").strip() or default_user_agent()
<<constants>>=
USER_AGENT_VAR = "SCHOLAR_USER_AGENT"
DISTRIBUTION_NAME = "scholarcli"
PROJECT_URL = "https://github.com/dbosk/scholar"
@

<<test functions>>=
class TestUserAgent:
    """The name scholar's requests go out under."""

    def test_default_names_scholar_and_project(self):
        agent = user_agent()
        assert agent.startswith("scholar/")
        assert "+https://github.com/dbosk/scholar" in agent
        assert "python-requests" not in agent
        assert "mailto" not in agent

    def test_contact_address_is_never_included(self, monkeypatch):
        monkeypatch.setenv("SCHOLAR_EMAIL", "me@example.org")
        assert "me@example.org" not in user_agent()

